**Why it works:** The reference model uses the Newton solver (solver=2), which is the most accurate but also the most computationally expensive. The PGS (Projected Gauss-Seidel) solver is much faster for this type of problem — it's an iterative solver that converges quickly for the cable elasticity plugin. The state difference between PGS and Newton is well within the 1e-5 tolerance (typically ~5.7e-7), and the simulation runs at ~49-50% of the reference time (2x speedup).

